trck <VERSION> — in-repo issue tracker

usage: trck <verb> [args] [options]

work with issues:
  new        create a new issue, body and all
  edit       rewrite an issue's prose
  mv         move an issue to a status
  start      alias: move to in-progress
  review     alias: move to in-review (and link a PR)
  done       alias: move to done
  set        edit metadata fields
  dep        add/remove a dependency edge
  label      add/remove labels on an issue

read the tracker:
  show       print an issue's metadata + body
  path       print the absolute file path of one issue
  which      resolve issue file paths back to issues
  list       browse issues as a nested forest (filterable)
  tree       alias for `list`
  ready      list unclaimed issues you can work on right now
  next       print the single best issue to work on next
  deps       draw the dependency DAG (lazygit-style gutter)
  serve      serve the tracker's page from a live process (loopback only)
  changelog  list issues shipped since a date/timestamp (release notes)
  diff       show what changed in the tracker between two points

maintain:
  check      validate consistency (nonzero exit on error)
  summary    regenerate SUMMARY.md
  html       write a self-contained HTML view of the tracker
  sync       share local tracker commits, and pick up what landed elsewhere
  repo       tracker maintenance (normalize, install-hook, …)
  init       scaffold a tracker into the current repo
  version    print the running trck version

global:
  --dir DIR  the tracker to act on, overriding discovery and $TRCK_DIR
  --ref REF  read the tracker from this git ref, overriding discovery and $TRCK_REF

`trck <verb> --help` for one verb's arguments, options and examples.
